cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lifelong Mapping and 3D Change Detection on Object-Level Scene Graphs"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ch Shreyash"
    given-names: "Shreyash"
  - family-names: "Farzana"
    given-names: "S"
  - family-names: "Wadekar"
    given-names: "Prajas"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrajasW/LM-3DCD-SG"
url: "https://prajasw.github.io/LM-3DCD-SG/"
abstract: >-
  Training-free relocalization and per-object change detection for a robot that
  revisits a changing indoor scene with a map from an earlier visit. The map is an
  object-level 3D scene graph. On every visit the robot builds a graph of what it
  currently sees, matches it to the map, recovers its pose without an initial guess,
  labels each object as static, moved, added, removed or not observed, and edits the
  map per object.
keywords:
  - mobile robotics
  - scene graphs
  - change detection
  - relocalization
  - lifelong mapping
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-01"
